  "caption": "Quinn's scan showed a heel spur. Quinn bought a cowboy hat, then limped through every first morning step, wondering if it had to come out.\n\nSpurs are common in pain-free feet. Heel pain usually comes from overloaded tissue on the sole of the foot, and it often settles with load-based rehab while the spur simply stays put.\n\nWhat can help: asking what changed in your standing, walking or shoes, progressive calf raises, trimming load spikes then rebuilding, supportive shoes and a gentle stretch before your first morning steps, and giving it 6–12 weeks.\n\nGet it checked for numbness or tingling, pain at rest or night, pain after a fall or pop, heel pain in a child, or a hot, swollen heel.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
